Archive the libraries in GNU ar's deterministic mode (D: uid, gid and mtime 0, mode 644) (solnix). hadrian packs every
static library with `ar q`, and binutils' ar records the build user: two builds of GHC 9.10.3 as nixbld10 and nixbld1 differed
in 84 .a files, and in nothing but those header bytes (ghc2 --check, 2026-11-12). Cabal wipes the same metadata itself
(Distribution.Simple.Program.Ar.wipeMetadata); hadrian has no such step.

--- hadrian/src/Settings/Builders/Ar.hs.orig
+++ hadrian/src/Settings/Builders/Ar.hs
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
         -- not added as a single file. This requires that we are using llvm-ar
         --
         -- See Note [Object merging] in GHC.Driver.Pipeline.Execute for details.
-        ifM (expr $ arSupportsDashL stage) (arg "qL") (arg "q")
+        ifM (expr $ arSupportsDashL stage) (arg "qLD") (arg "qD")
       , arg =<< getOutput
       ]
     , builder (Ar Unpack) ? mconcat
